<p class="prose" style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-secondary); margin-top:calc(-1 * var(--s2)); margin-bottom: var(--s3);">Total imports and the non-Gulf share are calculated from each country's Gulf-sourced value divided by its Gulf-wide dependency percentage above, not an independent Comtrade total-imports pull. Recomputed this way, the Hormuz-specific share lands at 35.8%, 65.8%, and 53.0% for India, Sri Lanka, and Thailand, matching the corrected dependency figures above by a different route.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-label">Model limitations</div>
  <div class="callout-body">Nitrogenous fertilizer (HS 3102) is Tier 2, Corroborated, in the Narrows model. Unlike crude oil and LNG, which have dedicated primary-source feeds behind them, this commodity is built from UN Comtrade bilateral pulls without an independent corroborating source layer. The dependency figures above should be read as directionally solid, not to the decimal point. The Oman correction itself is a routing fact, not a modelling assumption. Sur's geography relative to the strait is not in dispute, but the underlying trade values it is applied to carry the same estimation uncertainty as the rest of the model's fertilizer coverage.</div>
</div>

